From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: leave the attributes alone when FILE_BASIC_INFORMATION gives none

Purpose: setting a file's or folder's times no longer clears its hidden,
system and read-only attributes.
Windows behavior: in FILE_BASIC_INFORMATION, a FileAttributes of 0 means
the attributes are not changed (SetFileTime and SetFileInformationByHandle
with only times set pass 0).
Wine before: the attributes were always set, so 0 cleared the hidden and
system attributes kept in user.DOSATTRIB and made read-only files
writable. Windows 7's shell sets a known folder's attributes and then its
times (KF_FLAG_INIT), which left Links without any mark, and the shell no
longer read its desktop.ini.
Change: FileAttributes 0 leaves the attributes as they are; the times are
set as before.
Evidence: SHGetKnownFolderPath(FOLDERID_Links, KF_FLAG_CREATE |
KF_FLAG_INIT) in the Windows 7 shell prefix turned Links from 0x14 into
0x10; with this and 0121 it is 0x11, as on Windows 7.
Scope: everywhere.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
index 42c8253..e3aa066 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
@@ -5159,7 +5159,8 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtSetInformationFile( HANDLE handle, IO_STATUS_BLOCK *io,
             if (atime.QuadPart || mtime.QuadPart)
                 status = set_file_times( fd, &mtime, &atime );
 
-            if (status == STATUS_SUCCESS)
+            /* zero leaves the attributes as they are (SetFileTime, for one) */
+            if (status == STATUS_SUCCESS && info->FileAttributes)
                 status = fd_set_file_info( fd, info->FileAttributes,
                                            unix_name && is_hidden_file( unix_name ));
 
